Atoms is a mixed-license project, and this file is not the whole story.

It is the MIT grant for everything Atoms itself wrote in this repository: the
seven PHP packages under `packages/`, the deploy Action in `action/`, the
tests and documentation at the root, and — under its own copy of this grant at
`cloudflare/LICENSE-MIT` — the host JavaScript and guest PHP prelude under
`cloudflare/`.

Two things it does not cover:

  - A Worker assembled from `cloudflare/`, which links a PHP interpreter that
    is not in this repository and is GPL-2.0-or-later as a combined work.
    `cloudflare/worker/LICENSE` carries that licence and explains why it does
    not conflict with the grant below; `cloudflare/README.md` gives the full
    account.

  - Your own PHP application code. An Atom you write is carried into the
    runtime as data for an interpreter to read, not linked into it, and
    nothing here or in `cloudflare/worker/LICENSE` relicenses it.

There are no per-file SPDX headers. This file, `cloudflare/LICENSE-MIT` and
`cloudflare/worker/LICENSE` are the grant.

